      "DEBBIE: She’s my sister’s daughter. I have a responsibility here.\nHEATHER: What’s wrong?\nDEBBIE: Okay, Heather, listen to me. I’ve been where you are. I went to college. I was a Tri-Delt.\nDEBBIE: I did my share of partying and hooking up. They used to call me ‘Debbie Do-Anything.’",
      "AUDREY: It’s true. They do. They literally cry together.\nDEBBIE: Somehow I can’t imagine you crying, Stone.",
      "DEBBIE: I love the new place, Ellen.\nELLEN: Thanks. If we’d known you were coming I would’ve cleaned up.",
      "ELLEN: They call us ‘breeders.’ Isn’t that cute?\nDEBBIE: Adorable.",
      "DEBBIE: What?!\nELLEN: You didn’t know?"
    ]
